<urn:usf:requirement:operator-call-command-reservation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The predecessor operator owns one closed call tree containing call, call parallel and call compare and one reusable src/commands/graph-leaf-dispatch.ts boundary. Generic no-contact call remains local. Parallel and compare are proofblocking leaves owned only by provider-parallel-execution and require explicit --profile VERSIONED_IRI, --manifest PATH and --input PATH|-; payload content and module presence never establish authority. Each production leaf invocation uses one fresh single-invocation Node child and the parent never imports or caches provider-parallel.ts. The parent authenticates the implementation root and holds the shared primary-mutation lock before the child's first repository-module load. In the fresh child, rederive the exact selected work, current verified completion and newly current basis, authenticate one unique typed ProductionLeafRuntimeClosure, import only the graph-declared handler and reauthenticate its entry bytes. The child releases its shared lock and emits bounded prepared; the parent releases its lock and acknowledges; only then may input be consumed or inference begin. Exact process.execPath, a scrubbed fixed environment, bounded private control/result protocol and no fallback are mandatory. Missing, ambiguous, stale, drifted, cross-root, incomplete, byte-mismatched, moved or child-protocol authority refuses before contact. Later leaf work owns only its feature handler and cannot rewrite call.ts, graph-leaf-dispatch.ts, provider-leaf-dispatch.ts, help.ts, dispatcher.ts or cli.ts." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
