<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-host-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Model Codex ChatGPT and Claude claude.ai subscriptions as distinct first-party host transports, never as OpenAI or Anthropic API adapters. Bind executable/version, authenticated account mode, discovered or bounded candidate model surface, exact requested and actual identity, disabled fallback, absent API and alternate-cloud credential paths, and zero observed incremental paid cost while disclosing that the pre-existing subscription itself may be paid." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-model-closure> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-model-closure> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Join current authenticated host discovery to the frozen models.dev OpenAI and Anthropic model sets, keep aliases separate from model identities, and assign every candidate one explicit selected, eligible-unassigned, unavailable, unsupported, ambiguous or unqualified disposition. When a host exposes no exhaustive entitlement list, report the exact bounded denominator and unknowns rather than claim completeness." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive answer identity, usage, cache telemetry, cost diagnostics and useful monotonic intervals from exact bounded versioned host output bytes; missing fields remain unknown, model substitution or tool use fails closed, and live observations remain ignored route-local operational state rather than durable semantic authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-census-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-subscription-census-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require one explicit absolute operator-selected provider-state root and apply the completed exactOwnerControlledDirectory semantics without tightening or weakening them: lexical path equals realpath; invoking uid/gid ownership; owner-rwx; no world-write, special bits or symlink; nlink at least 2; and group-write only when reauthenticated passwd/group sources prove the current primary group has exactly the invoking user and no other explicit member. Apply the same rule to each fixed auth-file parent, require each recognized auth file to be an owner-only mode-0600 regular non-symlink nlink-1 file, recheck root, parents, file and membership sources for drift, and never print or copy credential content or selected paths. Launch only fixed absolute Codex and Claude metadata commands in independent Bubblewrap children with a tmpfs root, private user, PID and network namespaces, no host sockets or working tree, read-only system and exact auth-file projections, cleared environment, private scratch, bounded output and timeout. Exact absence of /usr/bin/codex or /usr/bin/claude is evaluated before auth-file absence and yields a route-local EXECUTABLE_NOT_FOUND observation with its frozen candidate denominator, even when that host's recognized auth file is also absent; it must not suppress an independently observable sibling host. A dangling or unsafe present host executable, unsafe provider-state root, unavailable Bubblewrap containment tool or observed containment/projection drift still refuses the census. Inability to answer without network remains unavailable and never widens this census into provider contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-host-readiness-diagnosis> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-host-readiness-diagnosis> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Extend the registered usf doctor interface with the same explicit absolute --provider-home selected for host census and the same completed exactOwnerControlledDirectory plus exclusive-primary-group rule, including fixed-parent/auth-file checks and drift reauthentication, then report bounded local readiness for the provider-state root, exact recognized auth files, Bubblewrap, Codex and Claude executable identity/version-check prerequisites and a no-network namespace self-check. Doctor must not launch Codex or Claude; only the exact Bubblewrap namespace self-check may spawn. Missing optional host executables remain unavailable facts, unsafe present identities or roots remain refusals, secrets and selected paths are never emitted, and readiness is not entitlement, provider availability, semantic qualification or inference authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
