<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before provider inference, use one separately authorized provider-owned non-inference account source to admit a trusted current exact-account tier receipt proving zero paid cost, paid usage disabled, automatic overage disabled, bounded quota applicability and source authenticity; self-authored assertions, promotional credit and model prose are insufficient." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-source-reuse> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-source-reuse> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Acquire one factual account observation per exact typed source identity keyed by transport, provider control plane, response-mapping digest, credential mode/name, non-secret credential-source identity and protocol, independent of product/profile. Require a separate profile/policy/privacy-bound authorization for acquisition or use; authorization movement invalidates only that profile's use/acquisition eligibility and never the factual observation. Reuse the current observation across authorized profiles and dependent models unless the mapping explicitly declares model scope, single-flight by the profile-independent source key while different sources contact concurrently, persist a bounded source-keyed failed-attempt retry deferral, and never hold the primary-mutation lock during contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
