<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-host-source-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive a subscription-host credential-source identity through a downstream no-network capability owned outside the completed census paths. It accepts one explicit provider-state root plus one exact current host-census authorization, applies the completed exactOwnerControlledDirectory plus exclusive-primary-group semantics without tightening or weakening them, authenticates the fixed provider credential file and executable without reading or hashing credential content, retains only canonical file-metadata/executable/authentication-mode digests, excludes the selected host/root/path, account identity and observation/authorization timestamps or expiry from credentialSourceIdentityDigest, and binds the expiring host authorization separately as a use gate. Missing, unsafe or moving identity remains not-observed/ineligible." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
