<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-dynamic-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive a canonical candidate-member identity for every frozen models.dev provider/model route and separately typed subscription-host candidate, then reduce the complete current authorized account-source and host-authorization set into one sourceSetDigest, one exact candidate-model economics binding and one terminal disposition per candidate without adding one graph row per model. Keep optional configured route-member identity separate for downstream calls. Bind explicit raw and normalized catalogue digests, exact provider/model/transport/adapter identity, every supported price dimension, sorted unsupported or conditional members, authorized account observation or retry deferral, entitlement, quota/reset, usage, paid/overage/top-up controls, spend cap, fallback, freshness and service tier. Zero sources is not-observed; more than one competing current source for a candidate is conflict-ineligible rather than selected by preference. Any unknown, conditional, stale, ambiguous, paid or fallback-capable fact is ineligible; catalogue zero is never account entitlement." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
