<urn:usf:acceptance:provider-census> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "One no-contact command family reports complete named denominators and bounded route detail, classifies every configured, disabled, excluded and local transport candidate exactly once, preserves one usable host when a sibling executable is absent, exposes no credential value, selected secret path or false availability claim, and constructs no adapter, provider engine or live authorization. The registered doctor surface predicts the exact local host-census root, auth, executable and namespace prerequisites without provider launch or contact while refusing unsafe present identities." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
