<urn:usf:acceptance:provider-account-receipt-acquisition> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The receipt owner's target activate mode derives one reusable ignored call-ceiling activation only from exact current construction authority and verified completion of the primary account-tier work and contract; no secondary work, permission, policy, proof lane, leaf or independently activatable contract exists. Activation refuses before credential access when owner authority, completion, graph, v2 command/runtime closure, policy or privacy moves, while unrelated source-key, catalogue, head-set and route movement leaves it current and two source keys may reuse it concurrently. Every target v2 acquire, verify or reduce invocation explicitly reauthenticates that activation and then its own exact source-local authorization and state. The modes authenticate one explicit bounded copy-on-write source-state head-set record, its exact explicit manifest heads and one frozen raw/normalized catalogue pair. API acquire authenticates one owner-private repository-local credential file, single-flights the exact accountSourceKeyDigest, takes one admission instant immediately before its graph-mapped non-inference contact, then takes one settlement/projection instant after the request settles and yields a sanitized observation or bounded retry deferral. API verify reauthenticates the explicit stored authorization, graph-selected account source, source-owned observation chain and current explicit credential identity; ambient environment is never authority. Subscription-host acquire performs no contact, derives one secret-safe host identity record whose stable digest excludes current authorization, then binds the current host authorization only in projection/use. Host verify separately requires provider home, exact host census and host-source identity. Competing selected-source revisions reconcile only through a successful fresh API observation or fresh local host identity naming every predecessor; a failed reconciliation contact records its retry-DAG attempt without a manifest successor and compare-and-swap-adds that attempt to the protocol-scoped deferral antichain while leaving the competing factual heads unchanged. Verify and reduce never preference-resolve. Every ok or ordinary deferred mode returns one content-authenticated manifest and a pure candidate-local full-denominator projection. Current factual source state suppresses needless reacquisition, persisted failed attempts defer only their source across unattended restart, unrelated sources remain parallel, and catalogue-only movement never causes account contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
