<urn:usf:provider-operation:route-economics-disposition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:configuredRouteJoinRule> "Authenticate the exact current config/providers.json file basis and derive every routeMemberDigest under urn:usf:provider-operation:route-member-key:1. A configured route can join only a models-dev-route candidate when route.provider equals candidate provider, route.model equals candidate model, route.adapterPackage equals the exact projection-bound normalized catalogue adapter package for that provider route, and candidate transport equals route.provider plus the ASCII suffix -api. Subscription-host candidates have no configured-route join under the current route schema. Zero matches sets configuredRouteMemberDigest null; exactly one sets that digest; more than one sets it null, emits CONFIGURATION_CONFLICT and makes only that candidate ineligible. Never choose by order, credential, preference, alias or installed state. configuredRouteCount counts the sorted unique digest set of all exact matches before per-candidate conflict disposition; unjoined configured routes remain visible only in their separate census denominator." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
