<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:inputRule> "Accept exactly none alone for a first-source acquisition, one through 32 explicit owner-private direct-child manifest paths in ordinary state, or exactly 33 only for an authenticated matching persisted overflow-recovery head set. Resolve each repository-relative path against the selected repository root and require the resolved absolute lexical path to equal realpath; authenticate regular non-symlink mode 0600 nlink 1 invoking-uid ownership, filename equals SHA-256 of exact canonical bytes, identical pre/post descriptor identity and closed schema before following any reference. Never enumerate the storage root or inspect Git/history/provider state." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetInputRule> "Accept exactly one explicit repository-relative .usf/provider-operations/source-state/heads/{scopeDigest}.json path whose scope digest is rederived from the current protocol, or none only after authenticating absence of that exact deterministic path. Existing records must be invoking-uid-owned regular non-symlink mode 0600 nlink 1 beneath the authenticated mode-0700 heads directory, use no-follow open, match pre/open/post descriptor identity and closed canonical schema, and name exactly the repeated explicit manifest heads. Never accept another scope, enumerate the directory or infer a pointer from history." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:closureBounds> "At most 32 ordinary or exactly 33 overflow-recovery supplied heads, 4096 unique recursively referenced post-checkpoint manifests, 128 parent edges on any path, 512 unique effective source keys, 65536 referenced in-closure source revisions and 67108864 aggregate canonical manifest/source-record bytes per invocation. Checkpoint basis heads are authenticated as bounded audit provenance but their pre-checkpoint parent/revision ancestry is not recursively reopened. Duplicate digests deduplicate; a cycle, missing required current record, bound overflow or digest/schema mismatch refuses before source contact or materialization. Reducer and manifest parent input remain capped at 32 even during recovery." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:sourceRecordRule> "Resolve every source record only beneath its graph-fixed ignored record root from its exact digest and variant, then authenticate closed canonical bytes. Paths are derived, never carried by the manifest. Unknown schema/protocol versions refuse; a graph-known older producerProtocolDigest remains historical provenance and is accepted only through an explicit compatibility mapping, never by equating it to the current CLI digest." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:sourceMemberBindingRule> "For every member rederive sourceKeyDigest as the exact accountSourceKeyDigest from urn:usf:provider-operation:account-source-key:1 and the graph-selected mapping. API members must exactly match the referenced observation or attempt accountSourceKeyDigest, its historical acquisition authorization, mapping/responseMappingDigest, transport, provider, credentialSourceIdentityDigest and protocol basis. Host members must exactly match the authorization-free host identity accountSourceKeyDigest, mapping, transport, provider, credentialSourceIdentityDigest and protocol basis. Current profile use authorizations and current host authorizations are never manifest fields; the reducer rederives and binds them separately for its selected projection. Tombstones retain the same key/mapping identity and valid predecessor closure. Any alias, splice or mismatch refuses." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:effectiveStateRule> "Each manifest is a complete multi-version snapshot with one bounded effective source-revision antichain per sourceKind plus accountSourceKeyDigest. Across supplied post-checkpoint parent closures, identical revisions deduplicate and a revision supersedes another only when every traversed previousSourceRevisionDigests link is present and authenticated in that closure. A checkpoint's retained effective members are new comparison roots without changing their factual/revision bytes; predecessor links leaving the checkpoint are opaque and never prove ancestry. Missing, pruned or pre-checkpoint-only ancestry is unknown and therefore incomparable, not an error or ancestor. Different effective revisions for one key with neither proven ancestral to the other are all retained as explicit concurrent conflict. No preference winner is selected, and conflict for one key does not prevent unrelated keys from advancing or being reduced." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:observationAttemptRule> "For one conflict-free API source a current successful observation or later policy-valid attempt may supersede exactly one effective prior observation/attempt source revision. Each failed contact's separate previousAttemptDigests are exactly the current maximal retry-attempt heads for the source and window across the supplied factual heads plus head-set deferrals; attemptOrdinal is one plus the bounded unique transitive retry-DAG event count. When the selected source has competing factual heads, only a successful fresh API observation may name every competing source revision and reconcile them. A failed reconciliation contact writes its bounded retry-DAG attempt, emits no successor manifest, compare-and-swap-adds the attempt to the head-set deferral antichain and leaves every conflicting factual head effective; profile authorization movement is projection-only and cannot reset the factual attempt DAG." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:preContactCapacityRule> "Before API contact or local host-identity derivation, compute the exact worst-case canonical successor under every manifest, per-key revision, key-count and byte bound. A new key must fit one additional member; a conflict-free selected key replaces at most one revision; a selected key already at the 32-revision conflict bound may proceed only as fresh-authority reconciliation naming all 32 and replacing them with one on success, while failure can persist only its separately pre-capacity-checked deferral and no manifest. Any other result that cannot be durably represented refuses before credential use/contact. Unrelated conflicts remain retained and do not serialize this check." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:tombstoneRule> "Removal emits a tombstone successor only from one conflict-free exact current effective revision for that source key. Tombstones remain in the complete snapshot, contribute to sourceSetDigest provenance, make the source inapplicable to candidates and prevent an unrelated stale head from resurrecting it; only an explicit successor of that tombstone may reactivate the same key. Competing heads must first reconcile through successful fresh source authority and cannot be preference-retired." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:successorRule> "Verify requires only the selected source key to have at most one effective revision, applies exactly one reauthenticated selected-source revision naming its one exact effective predecessor when present, and emits one full multi-version snapshot successor with every supplied head as sorted parents and basisHeadSetDigest while retaining every unrelated key antichain. Acquire does the same when the selected key is conflict-free, whether the new factual revision is a successful observation or an ordinary failed-attempt record; a first ordinary failure from none therefore creates an attempt-backed parentless genesis. If only the selected key is conflicted, acquire takes that source key's single-flight lock and may reconcile it only with one successful fresh authoritative API observation or fresh local host-source identity whose previousSourceRevisionDigests are exactly every competing effective selected-source revision; unrelated key conflicts remain retained. Only a failed conflict-reconciliation contact returns its bounded attempt without a manifest successor: all supplied factual heads remain unchanged and the attempt becomes a persisted deferral head. none permits only a parentless first-source genesis. Unrelated members and deferrals remain byte-identical." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:mergeRule> "Reduce any one through 32 authenticated heads by unioning source members, pruning only revisions proven to be authenticated ancestors of another same-key revision inside the supplied post-checkpoint closure, and retaining every bounded incomparable same-key revision. Emit one full multi-version snapshot merge whose sorted parents are exactly those heads; reuse one already-canonical head. If the next parent depth would exceed 64, emit a deterministic checkpoint with no parents, the same exact effective revision antichains, manifestKind checkpoint, checkpointBasisHeadDigests equal to the fully verified input heads and basisHeadSetDigest over that same set. The checkpoint resets traversal depth and makes no ancestry claim about revisions outside its retained members; any delayed pre-checkpoint branch is conflict-ineligible until fresh-authority reconciliation and can never preference-resurrect a tombstone. Conflicts remain explicit candidate-local ineligibility rather than a global reduction refusal." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:checkpointReplacementRule> "A checkpoint may enter the head pointer only as an exact compare-and-swap replacement for its fully authenticated input-head set, including the exact selected 32-head subset during overflow recovery. Authenticate every checkpointBasisHeadDigest file and its effective members at creation; later validation authenticates the checkpoint itself and treats that explicit basis set as audit provenance without recursively reopening pre-checkpoint ancestry. It is state-equivalent only to that consumed set. A later stale pre-checkpoint branch remains an explicit conflict requiring fresh selected-source authority; it is never preference-pruned or allowed to revive retired state." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:idempotenceRule> "If one supplied head already has the exact effective source members and no new revision, return that exact digest and write nothing. Otherwise derive createdAt from source/parent records, producerProtocolDigest from this exact protocol and all canonical bytes before no-replace creation; an existing identical target is verified and reused, while any different target bytes refuse." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:concurrencyRule> "Different accountSourceKeyDigests may acquire concurrently from the same immutable base and materialize branch heads. One source-key-specific single-flight lock at .usf/locks/provider-account-source-{accountSourceKeyDigest}.lock spans its authoritative contact or local identity refresh through no-replace successor materialization, so new same-key work joins or reuses that exact result and never blocks another key. The lock is one persistent invoking-uid-owned regular non-symlink mode-0600 nlink-1 inode opened no-follow beneath the authenticated mode-0700 .usf/locks directory and is never replaced while waiters may exist. Merge/successor computation holds no provider, Git or primary-mutation lock. Same-source branches already produced by crash or older writers may be reconciled only through fresh-authority selected-source acquire; verify refuses a selected-key conflict, while reduce retains it as an explicit bounded revision antichain and unrelated keys remain schedulable." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetRule> "The registered command persists one owner-private mode-0600 regular non-symlink head-set record at .usf/provider-operations/source-state/heads/{scopeDigest}.json beneath an authenticated invoking-uid-owned mode-0700 heads directory for unattended reuse. Its lock is the persistent nonreplaceable no-follow regular mode-0600 nlink-1 inode .usf/locks/provider-source-state-heads-{scopeDigest}.lock beneath the authenticated mode-0700 locks directory. With only that short lock held, compare-and-swap authenticates absent genesis or the exact expected record digest/generation, canonicalizes factual manifest heads and per-source failed-attempt heads to separate ancestry antichains, and atomically writes temp-file+file-fsync+rename+parent-fsync. Provider contact and projection never hold this lock; no directory scan, Git state, external content-addressable store, database or global lock participates." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetGenesisRule> "An authenticated absent record is updated only with expected digest null to generation zero and previousHeadSetRecordDigest null. Every successor requires expected digest equal to the current record content digest, generation current plus one and previousHeadSetRecordDigest equal to that digest. Existing unsafe, missing-after-observed, malformed or mismatched state refuses rather than being treated as genesis." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetAntichainRule> "CAS-add unions every pending returned head with the authenticated current heads, removes only a head proven by bounded authenticated post-checkpoint manifest ancestry to be an ancestor of another retained head, and retains every incomparable head. An ordinary update remains at most 32; adding one pending incomparable head to an exact 32-head state may persist exactly the defined 33-head recovery state and nothing may add a thirty-fourth. If the canonical antichain and all other record fields are unchanged, return the current record digest without a generation write." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetDeferralRule> "For each source key, authenticate the exact deferral heads consumed at contact admission. On settlement, CAS removes only those consumed selected-key heads and adds a returned failed attempt; within one window its previousAttemptDigests join every consumed maximal retry head, while a new policy-derived window starts a new retry DAG after the expired consumed heads are removed. Authenticate and prune only attempt heads proven by bounded retry-DAG ancestry, and retain every newly concurrent incomparable head on compare-and-swap mismatch. A successful selected-source observation or host identity removes only its consumed deferrals and adds none. Unrelated-key deferrals are byte-identical. A failed conflict reconciliation therefore survives process restart without pretending to be a factual manifest successor." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetDeferralCapacityRule> "Before contact admission, canonicalize and authenticate the current deferral antichain and require capacity to persist either one new selected-key attempt after replacing its exact consumed heads or, for a previously undeferred key, one additional entry within the 512-entry bound. A full unrelated-key deferral set refuses before credentials are consumed or contact begins; no entry is evicted, sampled or preference-selected. A selected key may join at most 32 same-window incomparable retry heads in one bounded attempt, after which those exact heads become ancestors of the single returned attempt." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetOverflowRule> "When CAS-add of one pending incomparable head encounters exactly 32 ordinary heads, first persist their exact sorted 33-head union as the defined recovery state; the pointer therefore survives process failure with no outside tribal pending state. Without the pointer lock, deterministically reduce the first 32 canonical head digests to one valid merge/checkpoint with at most 32 parents. Under the short lock, CAS the exact 33-head record to that reduction result plus the untouched thirty-third head, preserve deferrals byte-identically and ancestry-prune only with proof. The result has at most two heads. No head is dropped, sampled or preference-selected, and no reducer receives 33 inputs." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetReductionRule> "Ordinary reduction replacement is valid only when the expected record still contains exactly the consumed canonical head antichain. Overflow replacement authenticates the complete expected 33-head record digest/generation, consumes exactly its first canonical 32-head subset and retains the unconsumed head and every deferral. On compare-and-swap mismatch never union a derived result as a thirty-fourth pending head: reload; if 33 heads remain, derive or reuse the deterministic first-32 reduction against that exact record, and if another helper already reduced them, authenticate and continue from the resulting ordinary state. No command returns until its own successful factual result is represented by the pointer; never retry a stale replacement, discard a concurrent head or hold the pointer lock during reduction." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:outputRule> "Every ok mode and ordinary deferred acquire returns exactly one resulting sourceStateManifestDigest—reused, successor, reconciled, merged or checkpoint—which is the sole factual manifest input to economics reduction. A failed conflict reconciliation returns its attempt digest and no manifest result. Before return, the registered command compare-and-swap-adds every returned factual manifest head; any ordinary failed attempt is also added to the selected source's deferral antichain, while a failed conflict reconciliation adds only that deferral and leaves factual heads unchanged. It fully recovers any transient 33-head state and compare-and-swap-replaces only an exact consumed branch set with a freshly reduced head. No command returns ok/deferred or emits a projection while 33 heads remain; an interactive caller still receives every explicit immutable result digest." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:externalContact> "none" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "An ignored source-state manifest is explicit file authority for operational source currentness only. Its local pointer uses compare-and-swap, but neither artifact is an external content-addressable store, database, Git or GitHub authority, provider availability, semantic qualification or inference permission." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:DeterministicOperationalProjectionRule> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:inputManifestSchema> <urn:usf:provider-source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:inputSet> "Exactly one resulting content-authenticated source-state manifest digest emitted or reused by the source-state protocol, containing the complete canonical graph-known factual observation/attempt or stable host-identity snapshot. Separately derive and authenticate the exact current profile/policy/privacy account-source use authorizations and supplied current host-census authorizations for this projection; neither class is stored in the factual manifest. The reducer performs no implicit directory, history, credential or provider-state scan." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:sourceSetDigestRule> "SHA-256 of exact canonical sorted factual source-member records keyed only by accountSourceKeyDigest for both API and subscription-host variants, binding credentialSourceIdentityDigest and observation/attempt or host-identity digest with no profile use authorization, current host authorization, secret, path or response bytes. Candidate bindings separately hash their exact current use and host-authorization digests; the global factual sourceSetDigest cannot grant use." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:candidateJoinRule> "For each candidateMemberDigest admit exactly one applicable factual source joined to exactly one current matching profile/policy/privacy use authorization and, for subscription host, exactly one current matching content-authenticated host authorization. Zero yields not-observed/ineligible; ambiguity or more than one distinct applicable current source yields source-conflict/ineligible. Never choose by provider preference, array order, latency or cost." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:sourceApplicabilityRule> "A provider-http-account mapping applies only when candidate sourceKind is models-dev-route and candidate provider and transport equal that mapping's exact provider and transport; therefore the openrouter-current-key mapping applies only to openrouter plus openrouter-api candidates. A subscription-host mapping applies only when candidate sourceKind is subscription-host and candidate provider and transport equal that mapping's exact provider and transport. Model scope may then cover every model under that exact source mapping. No API source crosses to another provider/transport, no host source crosses to an API or other host lane, catalogueProvider never substitutes for provider, and configured-route membership is irrelevant to applicability." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:candidateCurrentnessRule> "Each candidate binding and disposition hashes only canonical applicable source-member records into candidateSourceSetDigest. The global sourceSetDigest is aggregate provenance only and cannot enter candidate, configured-route, run-authorization or qualification currentness. Unrelated source movement leaves candidate bytes and downstream authority unchanged." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:aggregateRootRule> "Partition candidateMemberDigest by its first two lower-case hexadecimal digest octets into 256 fixed buckets. For each kind and prefix, hash the canonical sorted candidateMemberDigest/recordDigest/sourceKind/provider/model/transport member array into memberSetDigest, embed it in the closed bucket record, then hash the complete bucket bytes. Every identity must rederive its candidateMemberDigest. bindingSetDigest and dispositionSetDigest each hash the exact ordered 256 bucket-record digests from 00 through ff. Empty buckets use the canonical empty members array and its memberSetDigest but retain distinct kind/prefix-bound bucket-record digests. Only affected candidate records and buckets change, and the identity index enables bounded filtered pages without opening every candidate record." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:bindingRecordPathPattern> ".usf/provider-operations/economics/bindings/{candidate-prefix}/{candidateMemberDigest}-{recordDigest}.json" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionRecordPathPattern> ".usf/provider-operations/economics/dispositions/{candidate-prefix}/{candidateMemberDigest}-{recordDigest}.json" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:bindingBucketPathPattern> ".usf/provider-operations/economics/binding-buckets/{candidate-prefix}/{bucketDigest}.json" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionBucketPathPattern> ".usf/provider-operations/economics/disposition-buckets/{candidate-prefix}/{bucketDigest}.json" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:projectionPathPattern> ".usf/provider-operations/economics/projections/{projectionDigest}.json" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:projectionStorageRule> "No-replace-write canonical candidate binding, disposition, bucket and projection records only at their exact graph-fixed ignored paths. candidate-prefix is the candidateMemberDigest's first two lower-case hexadecimal octets and the filename identities must exactly match authenticated closed canonical bytes. Authenticate every fixed ancestor as invoking-uid-owned mode-0700 real non-symlink directories, then create mode-0600 regular non-symlink nlink-1 files with temp-file+file-fsync+rename+parent-fsync and existing-byte equality on reuse. These files are disposable operational acceleration, not semantic, Git, database or external content-addressable-store authority; the exact frozen inputs can reproduce them." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:boundedOutputRule> "The receipt child returns only the compact aggregate, its 512 ordered bucket digests and at most the exact single-route rows selected by --route. It never serializes the full candidate arrays through the child protocol. The complete denominator remains authenticated by candidateCount plus the two bucket roots and is read through the exact bounded target urn:usf:command:providers-receipt-list:1; canonical output from either command must remain within the registered 4194304-byte child ceiling or refuse before writing a partial result." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:manifestMergeRule> "Require the source-state protocol to have reduced every explicit head to one reused, successor, merged or checkpoint manifest. Reverify that exact manifest and every current referenced source record by digest; never repeat head selection, scan state or preference-resolve a conflict inside candidate projection." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:reductionOrder> "Canonical candidate-member-digest code-unit order after O(source-count+candidate-count+binding-count) hash-indexed validation." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:concurrencyRule> "Each source may acquire independently; reduction is pure, no-contact and snapshot-bound, takes no provider/Git/global mutation lock, and reruns after any source or catalogue result without serializing other source acquisition." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:economics-source-set-reducer:1> <urn:usf:predicate:evaluationInstantRule> "Accept only the parent registered receipt invocation's mode-specific projection instant: settlement after API contact, post-identity settlement for host acquire, or post-input-authentication for verify/reduce. Apply it identically to every post-result authorization, attempt, observation, host and candidate expiry/currentness comparison and aggregate generatedAt; no inner clock read or caller historical override is permitted." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
