<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:timestampRule> "Capture attemptedAt once after the bounded attempt settles; require integer Unix epoch milliseconds and serialize attemptedAt/windowStartedAt/windowExpiresAt/retryAfter, when non-null, as RFC3339 UTC Z with exactly three fractional digits. windowStartedAt=floor(attemptedAtEpochMilliseconds/3600000)*3600000 and windowExpiresAt=windowStartedAt+3600000." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:jitterRule> "jitterMilliseconds is the unsigned big-endian first four bytes of SHA-256 over USF canonical JSON v1 [accountSourceKeyDigest,windowStartedAt,attemptOrdinal], modulo 10001." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:delayRule> "For retryable attemptOrdinal n in 1..5, delayMilliseconds=min(900000,30000*2^(n-1)+jitterMilliseconds). retryAfter=attemptedAt+delay except the fifth attempt sets disposition circuit-open and retryAfter=max(attemptedAt+delay,windowExpiresAt). Arithmetic uses exact safe integers and overflow refuses." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
