<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:satisfactionKey> "accountSourceKeyDigest-for-api-and-subscription-host" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:requiredCurrentBasis> "For API factual state: exact source key, selected mapping/response mapping, credential-source identity, protocol, historical acquisition authorization, authenticated account identity, acquiredAt/expiresAt and raw-response digest; current profile use authorization is separately rederived. For host factual state: the same source-key protocol, selected mapping and authorization-free stable credential/executable/authentication-mode identity; current host authorization and profile use authorization are separately reauthenticated. Every successful mode binds the exact resulting source-state manifest and its mode-specific projection instant." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:authorizationRule> "Each API acquisition/reuse and each subscription-host use requires its own current exact operational-activation/profile/policy/privacy AccountSourceAuthorization over the same source key and credential identity. Host use additionally requires the exact current content-authenticated host authorization separately from stable identity. Neither factual record grants another activation, profile or future use; activation/authorization movement invalidates only scoped use eligibility rather than the stable factual key." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:suppressionRule> "A current exact API observation suppresses contact until expiry or relevant key/mapping/credential/protocol/authenticated-identity movement; a current authorization-free host identity record suppresses local rederivation until its credential/executable/mode identity moves, while refreshed host and profile use authorizations are rechecked and bound only in projection. Missing/stale factual state enables one exact source-key single flight. Competing selected-source revisions require one fresh successful authoritative observation or host identity; a failed reconciliation attempt leaves the factual heads unchanged, is persisted in the head-set deferral antichain, and is reused by waiters and restarted orchestration." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:failureDeferralRule> "Every failed contact writes one bounded sanitized source-keyed attempt bound to the exact versioned retry policy and compare-and-swap-adds it to the protocol-scoped head-set deferral antichain before return. Until every current deferral head's retryAfter it is retry-deferred and cannot be scheduled; reaching the retry-DAG attempt ceiling opens the source-local circuit through the policy-derived bound, while terminal classes require relevant source movement. Authorization/profile churn cannot bypass the source-key window. Other source keys remain schedulable, and a successful selected-source result removes only the deferrals it exactly consumed." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:catalogueMovementRule> "Raw/normalized catalogue or candidate-set movement recomputes candidate economics and dispositions locally and never by itself reacquires an account observation." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:modeRule> "Acquire may perform API contact or local host identity derivation and may fresh-authority-reconcile only its selected key, with reconciliation success limited to a fresh API observation or host identity; unrelated source conflicts remain explicit and do not block it. Verify is local and requires only its selected key to be conflict-free plus exact API or host evidence. Reduce is pure and normally accepts one through 32 explicit heads; every mode may first recover an exact persisted 33-head overflow state by reducing only a canonical 32-head subset. Reduction retains every bounded same-key revision antichain without preference. Successful modes return exactly one resulting sourceStateManifestDigest and a full candidate-local projection only from ordinary state; a failed selected-key reconciliation returns only its bounded attempt and unchanged-head disposition." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:lifecycleRule> "Unattended start/watch/Hermes must pass the exact explicit owner-private protocol-scoped head-set record and its exact factual manifest antichain into every target v2 providers receipt invocation. The registered command compare-and-swap-adds each successful returned branch or failed-attempt deferral, and replaces only an exact consumed factual branch set with a newly reduced single head. Neither layer rediscovers state from a directory or Git. Scheduling authenticates the persisted source-local deferral antichain before contact, may run different unsatisfied source keys concurrently from the same immutable base, explicitly reduces branches, and may not repeatedly select a satisfied or deferred source." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:storageRule> "Routine authorization, observation, projection and satisfaction state is owner-private ignored operational state with no Git or semantic publication requirement." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-account-observation-satisfaction:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Operational satisfaction is not semantic work completion, provider availability, route qualification or inference authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
